Z||000000||sqoach||11-28-2001||03:48 PM||||It must be from the cold, but is this normal? When I hit a dip in the road, I hear this creaking coming from the front. Possibly the rear too. I don't really notice it on bumps, just the dips. Didn't happen before it got cold. And I don't remember it last year with my coupe, but who knows. It's rather annoying. Is it just something I have to live with?<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif">              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">               <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000001||84Bill||11-28-2001||03:55 PM||||spray liberal amounts of CRC or WD40 on all the rubber suspension parts. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||11-28-2001||04:00 PM||||Both my fieros creak and squeak in cold weather, bumpy roads and have done so since day 1.  Chalk it up to flexable enduro panels.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-28-2001||06:58 PM||||loosen the sway bar center mounts and put some silicone oil or brake grease in them.<P>don't spray it with petrolium. that may fix it for a little bit but oil damages the rubber. you'll accelerate whatever problem you've got.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
